invariant: INV-55
file: tls.c
catches: unit
reason: a user_canceled alert ends a run of KeyUpdates. It gives the caller
  no data, and ch_read reads past it, so a peer that sends one after each
  KeyUpdate sends KeyUpdates with no limit. A tcp-nonblocking caller that
  hands ch_read one record a call meets no quiet cap either. bin/unit sends
  a full run, a user_canceled alert and one KeyUpdate more, and requires
  CH_KEY_UPDATE_LIMIT.

--- old
        // ch_read's quiet cap bounds a hostile stream of these like any
        // other record that carries no data.
        return CH_OK;
--- new
        // ch_read's quiet cap bounds a hostile stream of these like any
        // other record that carries no data.
        t->key_update_run = 0;
        return CH_OK;
